[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-34291"] :question/problem "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]=5[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=5{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}-5{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 5{a}_{1}+(-1){a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-75645/selection/62b43ea31c4ff3c5f25d7fc27d40d146b0e62a1ba500ef6a5ded40d1556904df" :answer/id #uuid "348fd172-f1b2-5353-a075-bcbe10f768d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75645/selection/af921100fd32d4ea672fcdfa099bd71f2f8225759262a4bcfd2494855404ec7a" :answer/id #uuid "81f112b1-7432-568f-925a-18606d9533bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75645/selection/bbbe21838ae04407686e2d2232567005a9e02c28827ea8ec775cbe5901bc6001" :answer/id #uuid "22432655-8b0e-5ea7-a885-2a6d80e26128" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75645/selection/78a0fd963cbae5b8be475e85576b9ad6d9b0bd6c3ac47c14b1e71637cb0fa2f9" :answer/id #uuid "d1a83bd4-85a4-55da-9c83-3d4a142ad6a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75645/selection/57084255ac476e88f395c0be08a6ac4da2a99bcadcf8c3392d9e3db8630fd91a" :answer/id #uuid "af78d287-e340-5006-9cd0-12ccbefb9bec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75645/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "15fa3198-c889-5712-bd2a-b24c7f7ffbd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75645/selection/af921100fd32d4ea672fcdfa099bd71f2f8225759262a4bcfd2494855404ec7a" :answer-field/choices ["q-75645/selection/62b43ea31c4ff3c5f25d7fc27d40d146b0e62a1ba500ef6a5ded40d1556904df" "q-75645/selection/af921100fd32d4ea672fcdfa099bd71f2f8225759262a4bcfd2494855404ec7a" "q-75645/selection/bbbe21838ae04407686e2d2232567005a9e02c28827ea8ec775cbe5901bc6001" "q-75645/selection/78a0fd963cbae5b8be475e85576b9ad6d9b0bd6c3ac47c14b1e71637cb0fa2f9" "q-75645/selection/57084255ac476e88f395c0be08a6ac4da2a99bcadcf8c3392d9e3db8630fd91a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75645" :question/id #uuid "1429f843-5ee1-5edb-b1a8-4da2570633ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-75645" :question/problem "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=-2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=-2{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-2{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75645/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5130f54d-2a53-5373-81a6-355921ea7523"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75645"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105296/selection/472c01ac57180e3ed6081d43d43cd06037a2895440bc67ab5d9909a3674c7ba0" :answer/id #uuid "348be599-aa14-56e9-a0f5-522f07b90594" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105296/selection/c99bb28b73022e9fdecc8cd5b89d19cfb85b23f5d218f9d86c0f2631e859f720" :answer/id #uuid "d13a9ee8-7991-5dcc-aded-17b229330d37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105296/selection/bf33b9f3c4afe46bc220d4b78a0d6bc0bb678267f59a24f8f4fd04953b146be3" :answer/id #uuid "cebf84bf-2cab-5237-aa21-3119bc62546a" :answer/type :answer.t