only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105296/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5130f54d-2a53-5373-81a6-355921ea7523"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105296"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75640/selection/12465ee3248325371e1503c4334cc7c02b270ce634dfd4fe01b259c5e05afb8f" :answer/id #uuid "d06480f0-4ca1-5982-9636-b8d64f589ef8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75640/selection/ee518033e6828c0f6ab512a88666969288145cecbc43466cfd5168a4af1da795" :answer/id #uuid "491a9cb9-2bf9-5567-bc79-0ddca5afe073" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75640/selection/a70721455537754320ec584602adb8806561c3d17a1b69befeb2c6d62e67bb5f" :answer/id #uuid "da10b9e5-0c92-5b01-8c6a-e99dc823249d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "